<title>USA: Hurricane Danny update -- NWS.</title>
<headline>Hurricane Danny update -- NWS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following update on Hurricane Danny was issued by the National Weather Service (NWS) in Miami, Florida, at 0700 CDT/1200 GMT:</p>
<p>Position:  Lat.  29.6 degrees North</p>
<p>	     Long. 89.5 degrees West</p>
<p>	     (45 miles southwest of New Orleans, just east</p>
<p>	     of Port Sulphur, Louisiana)</p>
<p>Track:  northeast</p>
<p>Speed:  5 mph</p>
<p>Strength:  75 mph maximum sustained wind</p>
<p>Comments: A hurricane watch is in effect from Morgan City, Louisiana, to Destin, Florida.</p>
<p>After crossing Grand Isle on the tip of Louisiana's Mississippi River delta early Friday, the storm's next landfall will likely be in Mississippi or the western Florida Panhandle.</p>
<p>Hurricane-force winds extend 25 miles, mainly east, from the center of the storm.</p>
<p>Rainfall can be heavy (10-20 inches) and there is a possibility of isolated tonadoes along Danny's path.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk + 212 859 1621))</p>
</text>
